  "final_agent_text": "READY_TO_MODEL\nConfirmed understanding:\n\n- **Problem type:** 3-machine flow shop scheduling (5 jobs, 3 machines in fixed order).\n- **Objective:** Minimize the makespan — the completion time of the last batch (i.e., minimize the maximum completion time over all batches).\n- **Machines/vats:** 3 vats, each processes at most one batch at a time (no overlap on the same vat).\n- **Jobs/batches:** 5 batches, all available at time 0.\n- **Routing:** Every batch must pass through vat 1 → vat 2 → vat 3 in that fixed order.\n- **Processing times (batch i, vat j):**\n  - Batch 1: [3, 1, 1]\n  - Batch 2: [2, 1.5, 1]\n  - Batch 3: [3, 1.2, 1.3]\n  - Batch 4: [2, 2, 2]\n  - Batch 5: [2.1, 2, 3]\n- **Waiting:** A batch may wait (queue) between vats; no limit on wait time.\n- **No other constraints:** no release times, no deadlines, no fixed entry order, no other preferences.\n\nThe model will decide, for each vat, the order in which the 5 batches are processed, and the start/finish times of each batch on each vat, subject to:\n1. On each vat, no two batches overlap.\n2. For each batch, start on vat j+1 ≥ finish on vat j (flow-shop precedence).\n3. All times ≥ 0.\n\nMinimize the maximum finish time across all batches and vats.",
